# UIT S3T - LAB 3 AI GOVERNANCE RULES

## 1. STACK
- React 19 + Vite + ES2024.
- Use functional components and React Hooks.

## 2. NO LEGACY APIS
- Ban class extends React.Component.
- Ban ReactDOM.render.
- Ban defaultProps.
- Ban keyCode.
- Ban window.alert.

## 3. ZERO DIV-SOUP
- Prefer semantic HTML elements.
- Use main, section, article, header, dl, dt, dd, figure, and output where appropriate.
- Avoid unnecessary div wrappers.

## 4. ACCESSIBILITY
- Every input and select must have an associated label.
- Use React 19 useId() for generated label associations.
- Use semantic buttons and accessible interaction states.

## 5. STATE HYGIENE
- Immutable state updates only.
- Never synchronize derived filtering or sorting state inside useEffect.
- Keep state minimal and derive computed values during rendering.

## 6. EFFECT CLEANUP
- Every timer, event listener, and fetch inside useEffect must have cleanup.
- Use AbortController for cancellable asynchronous requests.

## 7. PERFORMANCE
- Use React.memo for PianoKey.
- Use shallowEqual comparison where appropriate.
- Keep callbacks stable with useCallback.
- Prevent unrelated piano keys from re-rendering.

## 8. AUDIO RESOURCE MANAGEMENT
- Manage AudioContext and OscillatorNode lifecycles correctly.
- Maximum 8 concurrent voices.
- Implement FIFO voice stealing.
- Release all active audio resources during cleanup.

## 9. CODE QUALITY
- Use ES modules.
- Prefer const over let.
- Use descriptive names.
- Keep components and utilities focused.
- No unnecessary dependencies.